r -> heartbeat RPC -> higher-term negative reply -> local contact refresh -> lease consumer\",\n          \"Ordinary replication higher-term reply -> stepDown channel -> Follower\",\n          \"Pending VerifyLeader -> false heartbeat vote -> main-thread Follower\",\n          \"Actual pipeline request -> transport timeout and failed-future publication -> pipelineDecode reads response without Error -> contact refresh before Success rejection -> possible lease consumption\"\n        ],\n        \"activity_classes\": [\n          \"A2\"\n        ],\n        \"behavior_ids\": [\n          \"b-initialize\",\n          \"b-heartbeat\",\n          \"b-append-contact\",\n          \"b-snapshot-contact\",\n          \"b-pipeline-contact\",\n          \"b-lease-consume\",\n          \"b-stepdown\"\n        ],\n        \"fact_ids\": [\n          \"fact-peer-contact-marker\"\n        ],\n        \"supporting_behavior_ids\": {\n          \"b-old-request-reject\": \"Actual receiver branch can produce a newer-term rejection; same-execution higher-term acquisition is still unknown.\",\n          \"b-negative-verify\": \"Independent negative-verification path can invalidate authority despite refreshed lease contact.\",\n          \"b-inmem-timeout\": \"Actual failed-future producer for the pipeline consumer; supplies a concrete no-delivered-response discriminator rather than assuming heartbeat rejection is not contact.\"\n        },\n        \"obligation_relation_kind\": \"consumption\",\n        \"counterevidence\": [\n          \"LeaderLeaseTimeout explicitly promises step-down without quorum contact, not on every rejected reply.\",\n          \"Source describes lease as heartbeat-connectivity checking rather than a read-only query lease.\",\n          \"Ordinary, snapshot and pipeline reply paths check higher terms before refreshing contact.\",\n          \"Pending VerifyLeader can step down on a negative heartbeat response.\",\n          \"TestRaft_LeaderLeaseExpire checks disconnected-peer role loss within two lease intervals; it does not specifically exercise delayed pipeline completion.\",\n          \"CommitTimeout drives ordinary/pipeline traffic even without client writes; after pipeline Success=false the implementation falls back to ordinary replication.\",\n          \"Ordinary in-memory AppendEntries propagates timeout errors and does not refresh contact on that branch.\"\n        ],\n        \"unknowns\": [\n          \"Requirement gap narrowed: AppendFuture.Response explicitly requires Error completion and success; the lease contract concerns actual contact, but an API mismatch alone is not a completed authority-loss finding.\",\n          \"Local execution gap: run a real in-memory pipeline timeout, correlate its request/future identity, observe Error and marker before/after actual pipelineDecode consumption.\",\n          \"Initial-prefix and same-history gaps: full cluster election, pipeline activation and isolated no-contact interval have not been executed. Remote processing without reply remains possible.\",\n          \"Endpoint gap: whether this refresh changes a scheduled lease decision or public leadership-loss timing remains unobserved; fallback replication and negative verification remain protective alternatives.\"\n        ],\n        \"priority\": 2,\n        \"trigger_rationale\": \"Reading the previously deferred pipeline producer revealed that failed futures are published and consumed without checking Error. This affects an existing principal-Fact producer, not an unrelated API inventory item. Next discriminator is a bounded actual-transport timeout comparison followed by lease consumption only under an explicit local state premise; broader elected-cluster history remains separate.\"\n      },\n      \"status\": \"active\",\n      \"parent_candidate_id\": null,\n      \"fork_reason\": \"\",\n      \"stage\": \"analyze\",\n      \"read_plan_id\": null,\n      \"material_ids\": [],\n      \"spec_task_ids\": [],\n 